 568:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** *                                     WAIT ON AN EVENT FLAG GROUP
 569:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** *
 570:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** * Description: This function is called to wait for a combination of bits to be set in an event flag
 571:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** *              group.  Your application can wait for ANY bit to be set or ALL bits to be set.
 572:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** *
 573:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** * Arguments  : pgrp          is a pointer to the desired event flag group.
 574:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** *
 575:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** *              flags         Is a bit pattern indicating which bit(s) (i.e. flags) you wish to wait
 576:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** *                            The bits you want are specified by setting the corresponding bits in
 577:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** *                            'flags'.  e.g. if your application wants to wait for bits 0 and 1 then
 578:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** *                            'flags' would contain 0x03.
 579:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** *
 580:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** *              wait_type     specifies whether you want ALL bits to be set or ANY of the bits to be
 581:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** *                            You can specify the following argument:
 582:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** *
 583:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** *                            OS_FLAG_WAIT_CLR_ALL   You will wait for ALL bits in 'mask' to be clea
 584:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** *                            OS_FLAG_WAIT_SET_ALL   You will wait for ALL bits in 'mask' to be set 
 585:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** *                            OS_FLAG_WAIT_CLR_ANY   You will wait for ANY bit  in 'mask' to be clea
 586:./ucos/Core/os_flag.c **** *                            OS_FLAG_WAIT_SET_ANY   You will wait for ANY bit  in 'mask' to be set 
